    {
      "id": "51a0dff7-8127-4c40-84bd-6ddef6fad628",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -736,
        -992
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 592,
        "height": 928,
        "content": "## 08-20-01 automate move out inspections and security deposit returns with AI\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow helps landlords and property managers turn a move-out inspection into a fair, itemized security deposit statement quickly and without disputes. A move-out is logged on a webhook with the deposit, any unpaid rent or utilities, and a list of inspected items. After validation the move-out is written to the MoveOutLog sheet as pending. An AI assistant reviews each item and decides whether it is a chargeable deduction or normal wear and tear, estimating a fair repair cost and severity. A deterministic engine then computes the deposit math: deposit minus approved deductions minus unpaid balances gives the net refund, or flags the amount the tenant owes. The landlord/manager gets a clear itemized statement that is emailed to the tenant, the disposition is saved back to the sheet, and the landlord is alerted on Telegram, with an extra email copy when the tenant owes money. Every morning a sweep finds move-outs still awaiting a decision and reminds the landlord, with an all-clear on quiet days.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Create a Google Sheet with a MoveOutLog tab using the exact column headers shown in the workflow nodes.\n- Connect Google Sheets, Gmail, OpenAI and Telegram credentials on the matching nodes.\n- Point your property system (or a form) at the lease/moveout webhook, passing tenant_name, tenant_email, unit, move_out_date, deposit_amount, unpaid_rent, unpaid_utilities and a damages array.\n- Set the daily sweep schedule, the landlord email address and the Telegram chat.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the AI prompts, the wear-and-tear rules, the sweep threshold, or swap Telegram for another channel."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
